From: bdx-iot <bdx-iot@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] imx8mp-debix-model-a: enable TEE/OP-TEE uclass in U-Boot proper

Without CONFIG_TEE/CONFIG_OPTEE, U-Boot has no driver to probe the
running OP-TEE instance via SMC, so it never performs the devicetree
fixup that inserts the "firmware { optee { ... }; };" node into the
FDT handed to Linux. The Linux kernel already has CONFIG_TEE=y and
CONFIG_OPTEE=y (via imx_v8_defconfig), but its optee driver can only
probe if that node is present.

--- a/configs/imx8mp_debix_model_a_defconfig
+++ b/configs/imx8mp_debix_model_a_defconfig
@@ -100,3 +100,5 @@
 CONFIG_SYSRESET_PSCI=y
 CONFIG_SYSRESET_WATCHDOG=y
 CONFIG_IMX_WATCHDOG=y
+CONFIG_TEE=y
+CONFIG_OPTEE=y
